interpretation as the quotient ring grading requires homogeneous cuts. -/
alias alg_parameter_cut_product_internal := Multigraph.incidenceCutTorProduct_internal_degree

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle` (global sections given an atlas)** Conditional.
For an actual integral scheme with an open cover realizing the incidence charts and
torus, sheaf gluing identifies its global sections with `IncidenceRing`. The glued
incidence scheme satisfies these hypotheses (`alg_incidence_global_sections`). -/
alias alg_global_sections_of_atlas := Multigraph.incidenceGlobalSectionsOfAtlas

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle` (actual scheme)** Proved for the scheme glued
from the original incidence quotient faces and their full higher intersections.
It is integral and its original Boolean charts cover it. Its independent projective
zero-scheme comparison is supplied by `alg_incidence_projective_zero_scheme`. -/
alias alg_incidence_scheme_cover := Multigraph.incidenceChartι_jointly_surjective

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle` (actual intersections)** Proved. Higher faces
are exactly the intersections of the original face opens in the glued scheme. -/
alias alg_incidence_scheme_intersections := Multigraph.incidenceFaceι_join_range

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle` (actual global sections)** Proved. The structure
sheaf of the genuinely glued incidence scheme has the original intersection ring
as its global regular functions. No atlas realization is an input hypothesis. -/
alias alg_incidence_global_sections := Multigraph.incidenceGluedGlobalSections

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle` (coefficient action)** Proved. The actual
scheme projection defines the coefficient action on genuine global sections,
and the global-section equivalence preserves the original coefficient map. -/
alias alg_global_sections_coefficients := Multigraph.incidenceGluedGlobalSectionsEquiv_coeff

/-- **`intro:tor` (actual global sections)** Proved. The original free complex
resolves genuine global functions with the geometric coefficient action, and
is minimal at the coefficient origin. The comparison of Tor with sheaf cohomology is
`alg_tor_isomorphism`. -/
alias alg_global_sections_resolution_minimal := Multigraph.incidenceGlobalFreeResolution_minimal

/-- **`alg:tor-isomorphism` (actual global sections)** Proved. The comparison
induced by the actual coefficient-linear global-section equivalence preserves
standard Tor products, defined by genuine multiplication lifts. The comparison of
the Tor product with the cup product on sheaf cohomology is `alg_tor_isomorphism_mul`. -/
alias alg_global_sections_tor_product := Multigraph.incidenceGlobalTorIso_mul

/-- **`intro:betti` (actual global sections)** Proved. The total Tor dimension
of genuine global functions with the geometric coefficient action is Q(G). -/
alias alg_global_sections_total_betti := Multigraph.sum_finrank_incidenceGlobalTor

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle` (homogeneous zero charts)** Proved. Normalize
one homogeneous coordinate to one at every vertex and impose the
multihomogeneous zero equations. These independent quotient charts are the
incidence charts. The global comparison is `alg_incidence_projective_zero_scheme`. -/
alias alg_homogeneous_zero_charts := Multigraph.incidenceHomogeneousZeroCharts

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle` (zero ideal descent)** Proved. Extension of
the original zero ideal on every face overlap is exactly the target zero ideal. -/
alias alg_incidence_zero_ideal_descent := Multigraph.incFaceIdeal_map_refinement

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle` (zero-scheme overlaps)** Proved. The actual
closed affine zero loci form pullback squares on all higher face restrictions. -/
alias alg_incidence_zero_overlap_pullback := Multigraph.incidenceZeroFace_isPullback

/-- **`alg:first-page` (line-bundle transition data)** Proved. All integral
multi-twists have explicit transition units satisfying the cocycle law. The
multi-twist sheaves are `alg_vertex_twist_sheaf`, with these units as their face
transitions (`alg_vertex_twist_face_frame_unit`); their cohomology is
`alg_vertex_twist_cohomology_states`. -/
alias alg_line_bundle_transition_cocycle := CechProduct.multiTwistTransition_cocycle

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle` (all face sections)** Proved. Every actual
face-open structure-sheaf restriction is the original quotient-ring refinement. -/
alias alg_incidence_face_sheaf_restrict := Multigraph.incidenceFaceSections_restrict

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle` (Ext degree zero)** Proved. Genuine Ext-defined
structure-sheaf cohomology in degree zero is the original incidence ring as an
additive group. This asserts no higher vanishing. -/
alias alg_structure_sheaf_H0 := Multigraph.incidenceStructureSheafH0

/-- **`alg:state-cohomology` (two-open derived comparison)** Conditional. Actual
section Cech classes compute genuine local degree-one Ext cohomology when that
degree vanishes on each open. For twist sheaves over a Noetherian base this vanishing
is `alg_twist_standard_local_vanishing`. -/
alias alg_two_open_cech_H1 := SheafTools.twoOpenSectionH1_comparison

/-- **`alg:state-cohomology` (actual long exact sequence)** Proved. The actual
structure sheaf has its genuine Mayer-Vietoris sequence in all degrees. -/
alias alg_structure_sheaf_mayer_vietoris := SheafTools.structureSheaf_mayerVietoris_exact

/-- **`alg:first-page` (terminal-open cohomology)** Proved. In every degree,
