alias alg_sheaf_terminal_cohomology := SheafTools.localSheafTop_comparison

/-- **`alg:first-page` (terminal-open naturality)** Proved. The all-degree
comparison commutes with the genuine maps induced by sheaf morphisms. -/
alias alg_sheaf_terminal_naturality := SheafTools.localSheafTopEquiv_naturality

/-- **`alg:first-page` (two-open global comparison)** Conditional. For a cover of
the whole space, ordinary two-open Cech H1 equals actual global Ext cohomology,
assuming degree-one local vanishing on both opens explicitly. -/
alias alg_two_open_global_H1 := SheafTools.twoOpenSectionGlobalH1_comparison

/-- **`alg:edge-bundles` (actual projective-line charts)** Proved. Each original
standard open of Mathlib's Proj of the two-variable polynomial ring is the
ordinary affine polynomial scheme, over any commutative coefficient ring. -/
alias alg_projective_line_charts := ProjectiveLine.standardOpen_comparison

/-- **`alg:edge-bundles` (actual projective-line cover)** Proved. The two original
standard Proj opens cover the whole projective line. -/
alias alg_projective_line_cover := ProjectiveLine.standardOpen_cover

/-- **`alg:edge-bundles` (actual projective-line overlap)** Proved. The restricted
Proj scheme on the genuine intersection is the affine Laurent scheme. -/
alias alg_projective_line_overlap := ProjectiveLine.overlapOpen_comparison

/-- **`alg:edge-bundles` (left structure-sheaf restriction)** Proved. Restriction
from the original left Proj open is the usual Laurent inclusion. -/
alias alg_projective_line_left_restrict := ProjectiveLine.left_sections_restrict

/-- **`alg:edge-bundles` (right structure-sheaf restriction)** Proved. Restriction
from the original right Proj open inverts the Laurent parameter. -/
alias alg_projective_line_right_restrict := ProjectiveLine.right_sections_restrict

/-- **`alg:edge-bundles` (original common base)** Proved. Both original Proj charts
preserve the original coefficient-ring structural morphism. -/
alias alg_projective_line_base := ProjectiveLine.chartι_toSpecBase

/-- **`alg:edge-bundles` (actual vertex product)** Proved. The original vertex-labelled
construction is Mathlib's actual indexed product over the original coefficient scheme. -/
alias alg_projective_product := ProjectiveLine.vertexProduct_comparison

/-- **`alg:edge-bundles` (original polynomial cover)** Proved. All original vertex
