/- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved (general graph maps; see also `alg_tor_isomorphism_graph_map_natural`). The aliases at the end of
this file cover three kinds of maps between multigraphs on the same vertex set:
* edge relabelings (edge bijections with per-edge orientation reversal and independent edge
  orders): `alg_relabel_incidence`, `alg_relabel_tor_product`, `alg_relabel_tor_one`,
  `alg_relabel_tor_trans`, `alg_tor_isomorphism_natural`, `alg_relabel_exterior_product`;
* the orientation signs ε_φ(e), as per-edge sign changes and signed edge relabelings:
  `alg_sign_incidence`, `alg_sign_tor_state`, `alg_tor_isomorphism_sign`,
  `alg_signed_relabel_chart`, `alg_signed_relabel_tor_state`,
  `alg_tor_isomorphism_signed_natural`;
* edge maps that need not be injective, with the Tor map derived along the (non-flat)
  coefficient ring map: `alg_derived_ring_map_eq`, `alg_edge_map_incidence`,
  `alg_edge_map_tor_state`, `alg_tor_isomorphism_edge_map_natural`.
* signed edge maps, combining both: `alg_signed_edge_map_chart`, `alg_signed_edge_map_tor_state`,
  `alg_tor_isomorphism_signed_edge_map_natural`.
Vertex bijections are covered on the algebra side (`alg_vertex_relabel_incidence`,
`alg_vertex_relabel_tor_state`, `alg_vertex_relabel_tor_product`, `alg_vertex_relabel_tor_trans`);
on the geometric side the scheme isomorphism, the transport of the twist sheaves, the exterior
bundles and their cohomology are formalized (`alg_vertex_scheme_perm`, `alg_vertex_twist_perm`,
`alg_vertex_exterior_cohomology`), and the naturality square holds
(`alg_tor_isomorphism_vertex_natural`, through the multi-twist state formula
`alg_vertex_twist_state_formula`). The disjoint-union isomorphism
𝒰_{G⊔H} ≅ 𝒰_G ⊗ 𝒰_H is `alg_disjoint_union_tensor`, with its coefficient, symmetry, associativity
and unit compatibilities. Vertex maps that identify vertices are covered on the algebra side:
incidence ring maps, Tor maps preserving products, units and composition, and degree zero on the
cycle-compatibility algebra (`alg_vertex_map_incidence`, `alg_vertex_map_tor_product`,
`alg_vertex_map_cycle_zero`, `alg_vertex_map_cycle_product_zero`), and in every Tor degree they
preserve edge-set components and vanish on colliding states (`alg_vertex_map_collision_zero`), with
the explicit state formula on non-colliding states (`alg_vertex_map_tor_state_formula`). On the
geometric side the pullback along a_φ of the twist sheaves and of exterior bundle cohomology is
constructed (`alg_vertex_twist_pullback`, `alg_vertex_map_exterior_pullback`); the naturality square
holds on colliding pieces (`alg_tor_isomorphism_vertex_map_collision`) and in general
(`alg_tor_isomorphism_vertex_map_natural`, through the multi-twist state formula for the pullback
`alg_vertex_map_twist_state_formula`). -/

/-- **`alg:cycle-product`** Proved, with `alg_cycle_algebra` and `alg_cycle_algebra_tor`. Row 0
of the state-sum table, β_{0,q}, counts the cycle unions with q edges (every vertex of degree 0
or 2), and cycle unions are in bijection with collections of vertex-disjoint simple cycles. The
graded ring isomorphism 𝒰_G/(S_G)_+𝒰_G ≅ ℂ[z_C]/(z_C z_D) is `alg_cycle_algebra`. -/
theorem alg_cycle_product [DecidablePred G.IsCycleCollection] :
    (∀ q, G.betti 0 q = (Finset.univ.filter fun S : Finset E =>
      S.card = q ∧ ∀ v, G.deg S v = 0 ∨ G.deg S v = 2).card) ∧
    (Finset.univ.filter G.IsCycleCollection).card = (Finset.univ.filter G.IsCycleUnion).card :=
  ⟨G.betti_zero_eq_card, G.card_cycleCollections⟩

