for small nonzero p it gives exactly wt(S) distinct simple admissible solutions, and different
states give different solutions. The chart coordinate π is the paper's w, so Φ is the map
w ↦ f; simplicity uses the determinant argument `isSimple_of_det_normC` rather than a Schur
complement. -/
alias sf_normal_form := Multigraph.exists_powerMap_normal_form

