/-- **`sf:boundary-algebra`** Proved. The special fiber local algebra has length wt(S). -/
alias sf_state_fiber_length := Multigraph.length_stateFiber

/-- **`sf:boundary-algebra`** Proved. For a state, the parameter germs form a regular sequence in
the analytic germ algebra: the special fiber is a complete intersection. -/
alias sf_state_fiber_regular := Multigraph.isRegular_powerMapGerm

/-- **`sf:boundary-algebra`, `sf:normal-form`** Proved. In the vertex coordinate f = Φ(w) of a
power-map chart, the germs modulo the parameter functions p_i ∘ Φ⁻¹ form the same boundary
algebra. -/
alias sf_vertex_fiber_equiv := Multigraph.IsPowerMapChart.vertexFiberEquiv

/-- **`sf:boundary-algebra`** Proved, with the ramification index read as the analytic vanishing
order: along the i-th coordinate axis the parameter p_i vanishes to order r_i. -/
alias sf_ramification_index := Multigraph.analyticOrderAt_powerMap_single

/-- **`sf:boundary-algebra`** Proved. The same vanishing order r_i along the i-th axis of the
vertex coordinate. -/
alias sf_ramification_index_vertex := Multigraph.IsPowerMapChart.analyticOrderAt_vertexParam_single

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex bijections). A vertex bijection, with edges and
coefficients unchanged, induces an isomorphism of incidence rings compatible with the identity of
the coefficient ring. -/
alias alg_vertex_relabel_incidence := Multigraph.VertexRelabel.incidenceEquiv_coeffHom

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex bijections). The induced Tor isomorphism (Mathlib
functoriality of the derived functor) permutes the state cohomology with the Koszul sign of the
vertex permutation on the active vertices. -/
alias alg_vertex_relabel_tor_state := Multigraph.VertexRelabel.incidenceTorFullState_vertexRelabel_apply

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex bijections). It preserves the Tor product. -/
alias alg_vertex_relabel_tor_product := Multigraph.VertexRelabel.incidenceTorVertexRelabel_product

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex bijections). It respects composition. -/
alias alg_vertex_relabel_tor_trans := Multigraph.VertexRelabel.incidenceTorVertexRelabel_trans

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved auxiliary. The Koszul sign of a vertex permutation is
nontrivial: a transposition of two active vertices gives −1. -/
alias alg_vertex_perm_sign_swap := Multigraph.vertexPermSign_swap

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex bijections, geometric side). The coordinate map
a_ψ : (P¹)^W → (P¹)^V permuting the factors is an isomorphism of schemes. -/
alias alg_vertex_scheme_perm := Multigraph.vertexSchemePermIso

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex bijections, geometric side). Ext-defined sheaf
cohomology is transported along the induced equivalence of abelian sheaf categories. The
transport of the twist sheaves and the exterior bundle is not formalized. -/
alias alg_vertex_sheaf_h_perm := Multigraph.vertexSheafHPerm

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. For the disjoint union of multigraphs,
𝒰_{G⊔H} ≅ 𝒰_G ⊗_ℂ 𝒰_H as ℂ-algebras. -/
alias alg_disjoint_union_tensor := Multigraph.incidenceSumEquiv

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. The isomorphism is compatible with the coefficient maps through
S_{G⊔H} ≅ S_G ⊗ S_H. -/
alias alg_disjoint_union_coeff := Multigraph.incidenceSumEquiv_coeffHom

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. It is compatible with the symmetry of disjoint union. -/
alias alg_disjoint_union_comm := Multigraph.incidenceSumEquiv_sumComm

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. It is compatible with the associativity of disjoint union. -/
alias alg_disjoint_union_assoc := Multigraph.incidenceSumEquiv_sumAssoc

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. The empty graph has 𝒰 = ℂ, and the unit isomorphism
𝒰_{G⊔∅} ≅ 𝒰_G is the one induced by the oriented isomorphism G ⊔ ∅ ≅ G. -/
alias alg_disjoint_union_unit := Multigraph.incidenceSumEmptyEquiv_eq_sumEmpty

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `supp:functoriality`** Partial (signed edge maps with vertices fixed).
A signed edge map copies the coefficients of an image edge to every edge above it with the
orientation sign: the chart equation of e goes to ε_φ(e) times the chart equation of φ(e), the
paper's a_φ^* b_e = ε_φ(e) b_{φ(e)}. -/
alias alg_signed_edge_map_chart := Multigraph.SignedEdgeMap.rename_varSignHom_incChartEq

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (signed edge maps with vertices fixed). Its Tor map, the
derived ring map along the signed coefficient ring map, is the sign change followed by the
unsigned edge map. -/
alias alg_signed_edge_map_tor_comp := Multigraph.SignedEdgeMap.incidenceTorSignedEdgeMapHom_eq_comp

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (signed edge maps with vertices fixed). The state of S goes to
the wedge sign times ∏_{e∈S} ε_φ(e) times the state of φ(S) when φ is injective on S, and to zero
otherwise. -/
alias alg_signed_edge_map_tor_state := Multigraph.SignedEdgeMap.incidenceTorFullState_signedEdgeMap

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (signed edge maps with vertices fixed). It preserves the Tor
product. -/
alias alg_signed_edge_map_tor_product := Multigraph.SignedEdgeMap.incidenceTorSignedEdgeMap_product

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (signed edge maps with vertices fixed). It respects
composition, the signs multiplying along the edge map. -/
alias alg_signed_edge_map_tor_trans := Multigraph.SignedEdgeMap.incidenceTorSignedEdgeMap_trans

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `alg:tor-isomorphism`** Partial (signed edge maps with vertices fixed).
The Tor isomorphism with exterior bundle cohomology is natural for signed edge maps. -/
alias alg_tor_isomorphism_signed_edge_map_natural :=
  Multigraph.SignedEdgeMap.incidenceTorExteriorEquiv_signedEdgeMap

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved example. For two parallel loops mapped onto one loop with
opposite orientation signs, the nonzero sum of the two loop classes maps to zero. -/
alias alg_signed_edge_map_loops := Multigraph.loopPairMap_flip_loopClass

/-- **`alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved auxiliary (comparison maps between binary covers). For an
injective map of direction sets with cell opens contained in the target cells, forgetting the
other directions (l, r ↦ 1, e ↦ 0, with explicit relabelling signs) is a chain map of the cell
sheaf complexes preserving the augmentation. -/
alias alg_cover_refinement_augmentation := SheafTools.BinaryCells.relabelSheafComplex_augmentation

/-- **`alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved auxiliary. The standard products computed through two binary
cover families agree when their concatenation, whose cell opens are the intersections, has
relatively acyclic cell terms. -/
alias alg_standard_class_cup_concat := SheafTools.BinaryCells.actualStandardClassCup_concat

/-- **`alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved (independence of the binary cover). On the product of
projective lines over a Noetherian base, the standard product on twist cohomology computed
through any binary cover family with covering charts and affine cell opens is the standard
product of the standard coordinate cover. -/
alias alg_vertex_cup_cover_independent := ProjectiveLine.vertexTwistStandardClassCup_cover_independent

/-- **`alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved. In particular the product does not depend on the order of
the vertices in the standard cover. -/
alias alg_vertex_cup_reindex := ProjectiveLine.vertexTwistStandardClassCup_reindex

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex maps). A vertex map, possibly identifying vertices,
with edges unchanged, induces by pullback of functions along a_φ an algebra map of incidence rings
compatible with the identity of the coefficient ring. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_incidence := Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceHom_coeffHom

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex maps). The induced map of actual Tor (Mathlib
functoriality of the derived functor) preserves the Tor product, by a chain-level comparison. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_tor_product := Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceTorMap_product

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex maps). It preserves the unit. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_tor_one := Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceTorMap_one

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex maps). It respects composition. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_tor_trans := Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceTorMap_trans

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `alg:cycle-product`** Partial (vertex maps). On the cycle-compatibility
algebra the class z_C goes to a nonzero multiple of z_{φ(C)} when φ is injective on the vertices of
C. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_cycle_class := Multigraph.VertexMap.exists_ne_zero_cycleAlgebraHom_X

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `alg:cycle-product`** Partial (vertex maps). The class z_C goes to zero
exactly when φ identifies two vertices of C. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_cycle_zero := Multigraph.VertexMap.cycleAlgebraHom_X_eq_zero_iff

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `alg:cycle-product`** Partial (vertex maps). Identifying a vertex of
each of two vertex-disjoint cycles C, D sends the nonzero product z_C z_D to zero. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_cycle_product_zero := Multigraph.VertexMap.cycleAlgebraHom_acceptance

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex bijections, geometric side). The pushforward along the
scheme isomorphism permuting the factors of (ℙ¹)^V carries the twist sheaf O(a) to the twist sheaf
with the permuted twist; the isomorphism is glued from the transported chart frames. -/
alias alg_vertex_twist_perm := Multigraph.vertexTwistPermIso

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex bijections, geometric side). The induced isomorphism of
the exterior bundles. -/
alias alg_vertex_exterior_perm := Multigraph.VertexRelabel.exteriorPermIso

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex bijections, geometric side). The induced linear
isomorphism of exterior bundle cohomology, componentwise the transport of twist cohomology. -/
alias alg_vertex_exterior_cohomology := Multigraph.VertexRelabel.exteriorCohomologyVertexRelabel

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved auxiliary (vertex bijections). The
naturality square from the multi-twist state formula `VertexTwistStateFormula`; the formula is
`alg_vertex_twist_state_formula` and the unconditional square `alg_tor_isomorphism_vertex_natural`. -/
alias alg_tor_isomorphism_vertex_natural_of :=
  Multigraph.VertexRelabel.incidenceTorExteriorEquiv_vertexRelabel_of

/-- **`alg:theta-special-value`** Proved. For a connected graph and every γ in a commutative ring,
θ_G(1, γ) = Σ_{k=0}^{ν} C(ν, k) f_{2k}(γ), by contraction of a spanning tree to the bouquet of ν
loops. -/
alias alg_theta_special_value_sum := Multigraph.thetaGen_eval_one_of_connected

/-- **`alg:theta-special-value`** Proved. With γ = ξ − ξ⁻¹ over a field (1 + ξ² ≠ 0 is needed only
for ν = 0), θ_G(1, γ) = (ξ + ξ⁻¹)^{ν−1} (ξ^{ν−1} + ξ^{1−ν}). -/
alias alg_theta_special_value := Multigraph.thetaGen_eval_one_of_connected_sub_inv

/-- **`alg:theta-special-value`** Proved auxiliary. The closed form
f_d(ξ − ξ⁻¹) = (ξ^d + (−1)^d ξ^{2−d}) / (1 + ξ²). -/
alias alg_theta_f_closed_form := fGen_sub_inv

/-- **`alg:theta-special-value`** Proved. At γ = 2, with ξ = 1 + √2,
θ_G = (4 + 2√2)^{ν−1} + (4 − 2√2)^{ν−1}. -/
alias alg_theta_special_value_two := Multigraph.theta_eq_lam_mu_zpow_of_connected

/-- **`alg:state-dimensions`** Proved. The dimension of E_1^{−q,j}(G) = H^j(X_G, ∧^q F_G^∨), the
Ext-defined cohomology of the exterior bundle, is Σ_{|S|=q, v(S)=j} wt(S), and the total over all
q, j is Q(G). -/
alias alg_state_dimensions := Multigraph.exteriorBundleCohomology_stateDimensions

/-- **`alg:state-dimensions`** Proved. Over every nontrivial Noetherian base the exterior bundle
cohomology is free of rank the state dimension. -/
alias alg_exterior_bundle_finrank := Multigraph.exteriorBundleCohomology_finrank

/-- **`alg:k4-resolution`** Proved. For K₄ the nonzero graded Betti numbers, the dimensions of the
internal Tor pieces, are β_{0,0} = 1, β_{0,3} = 4, β_{0,4} = 3, β_{1,5} = 24 and β_{2,6} = 16:
the resolution 0 → S(−6)^16 → S(−5)^24 → S ⊕ S(−3)^4 ⊕ S(−4)^3 → 𝒰_{K₄} → 0. -/
alias alg_k4_graded_betti := Examples.K4_graded_betti

/-- **`alg:k4-section`** Proved. The minimal module generators of 𝒰_{K₄} are 8: the unit, four
triangle classes in degree 3 and three square classes in degree 4. -/
alias alg_k4_module_generators := Examples.K4_module_generator_counts

/-- **`alg:k4-section`** Proved. In 𝒰_{K₄}/S_+𝒰_{K₄} every product of two non-unit generator
classes vanishes, because any two cycles of K₄ share a vertex. -/
alias alg_k4_generator_products := Examples.K4_generator_mul_eq_zero

/-- **`real:edge-branches`, `supp:edge-branches`** Proved. Both real edge branches are analytic on
the open positive quadrant of (F_i, F_j), are zeros of the edge equations, and the edge Jacobian
has positive determinant on the positive branch and negative determinant on the negative branch. -/
alias real_edge_branches_analytic := BP.edgeBranches_analytic_jacobian

/-- **`real:vertex-map`, `supp:vertex-map`** Proved. On a real sign sector the sector messages and
fields are real analytic, the vertex coordinates are real analytic on the open set of positive total
fields, the two correspondences are mutually inverse restrictions, and nondegeneracy of the BP
solution is equivalent to injectivity of the derivative of the vertex map. -/
alias real_vertex_map_analytic := Multigraph.sectorVertexMap_analytic

/-- **`real:vertex-map`** Proved. An admissible solution is simple exactly when the derivative of
the sector field map at its vertex coordinates is injective. -/
alias real_vertex_map_nondegeneracy := Multigraph.isSimpleSolution_iff_fderiv_sectorField_injective

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex maps). In every Tor degree the Tor map of a vertex map
commutes with the orientation sign action of the edges. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_tor_sign := Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceTorMap_sign

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex maps). Over ℂ the Tor map preserves the edge-set
components: the sign characters ∏_{e∈S} ε_e separate edge sets. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_edge_set := Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceTorMap_mem_edgeSetPiece

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex maps). The Tor map preserves the internal degree in
every Tor degree. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_internal_degree := Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceTorMap_mem_internalPiece

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex maps). If φ identifies two active vertices of an edge
set S, the Tor map sends every element of the S-component to zero, in every Tor degree: the image
of S would have a larger homological degree. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_collision_zero := Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceTorMap_eq_zero_of_not_injOn

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved auxiliary (vertex bijections). The multi-twist state formula:
the transport of Ext-defined twist cohomology along the scheme isomorphism permuting the factors
acts on state coordinates by the relabeling with the Koszul sign of the permutation on the active
vertices, in every degree. -/
alias alg_vertex_twist_state_formula := Multigraph.vertexTwistStateFormula

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved (vertex bijections). The Tor isomorphism
with exterior bundle cohomology is natural for vertex bijections: the Tor map induced by the
incidence ring isomorphism corresponds to the cohomology map induced by the scheme isomorphism. -/
alias alg_tor_isomorphism_vertex_natural :=
  Multigraph.VertexRelabel.incidenceTorExteriorEquiv_vertexRelabel

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved (vertex bijections). The geometric map preserves the exterior
cohomology products. -/
alias alg_vertex_exterior_product := Multigraph.VertexRelabel.exteriorCohomologyVertexRelabel_product

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved example. The transport sends the constant section 1 of H^0(O)
to 1. -/
alias alg_vertex_twist_perm_unit := Multigraph.vertexTwistHPerm_unit

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved example. On two vertices the swap multiplies the H^2 class of
O(−2,−2) with unit state by −1. -/
alias alg_vertex_twist_perm_swap := Multigraph.vertexTwistHPerm_swap

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. The transport along a composite permutation is the composite of
the transports. -/
alias alg_vertex_twist_perm_trans := Multigraph.vertexTwistHPerm_trans

/-- **`prop:bp-family`** Proved (generic finite étaleness). For a loopless graph there is a nonzero
s ∈ ℂ[a, b], divisible by ∏ a_e ∏ b_i, such that over ℂ[a, b][1/s] the localized coordinate ring of
the admissible BP family is finite, free of rank Q(G) and étale, and every complex parameter with
s ≠ 0 has exactly Q(G) admissible solutions, all simple. -/
alias prop_bp_family_finite_etale := Multigraph.familyRing_finite_etale

/-- **`prop:bp-family`** Proved. The same holds with the rank given by any generic degree N. -/
alias prop_bp_family_finite_etale_degree := Multigraph.familyRing_finite_etale_of_hasGenericDegree

/-- **`prop:bp-family`** Proved. The parameter map ℂ[a, b] → coordinate ring of the family is
injective (the family dominates the parameter space). -/
alias prop_bp_family_dominant := Multigraph.paramToFamily_injective

/-- **`eq:belief-cover`** Proved. The belief ring is finite, free of rank 2^m and étale over the
belief base ring. -/
alias eq_belief_cover_finite_etale := Multigraph.beliefRing_finite_etale

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle`, `supp:vector-bundle`** Proved (the evaluation map). The chart
evaluation maps glue to a morphism of sheaves of modules O^{4m} → F_G = ⊕_e L_e on (ℙ¹)^V, which on
every chart subopen is the chart evaluation map in the chart frames. -/
alias alg_vector_bundle_evaluation_sheaf := Multigraph.incEvaluationSheafMap_chart

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle`, `supp:vector-bundle`** Proved (the kernel sheaf). The kernel
K of the glued evaluation map restricted to each standard chart is the free sheaf of rank 3m,
compatibly with the chart kernel coordinates. -/
alias alg_kernel_sheaf_chart := Multigraph.incKernelChartIso_chart

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle`, `supp:vector-bundle`** Proved. The transitions of K between
charts are the kernel transitions g_{τσ} of the chart trivializations of Z_G. -/
alias alg_kernel_sheaf_transition := Multigraph.incKernelSheafTransition_eq

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle`, `supp:vector-bundle`** Proved. The transitions of the face
trivializations of the incidence zero scheme are the linear substitutions Sym(g^∨) given by the
transitions of K. -/
alias alg_kernel_sheaf_zero_scheme := Multigraph.incFaceKernelTriv_transition_kernelSheaf

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle`, `supp:vector-bundle`** Proved. The kernel sheaf sequence
0 → K → O^{4m} → F_G → 0 of sheaves of modules on (ℙ¹)^V is short exact: the glued evaluation map
is an epimorphism, being surjective on sections over every chart subopen. -/
alias alg_kernel_sheaf_short_exact := Multigraph.incKernelShortComplex_shortExact

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle`, `supp:vector-bundle`** Proved. On every standard chart the
sequence splits, the section being the chart evaluation section. -/
alias alg_kernel_sheaf_chart_splitting := Multigraph.incKernelChartSplitting

/-- **`supp:boundary-algebra`** Proved. Through p_i ↦ c_i w_i^{r_i} (c_i ≠ 0, r_i > 0) the analytic
germ algebra ℂ{w} is a free ℂ{p}-module with basis the monomials w^α, α in the box α_i < r_i. -/
alias supp_boundary_family_basis := BoundaryAlgebra.familyBasis

/-- **`supp:boundary-algebra`** Proved. Its rank is ∏ r_i. -/
alias supp_boundary_family_rank := BoundaryAlgebra.finrank_paramGerms

/-- **`supp:boundary-algebra`, `sf:boundary-algebra`** Proved. For a state S and the parameters
p_i = (−1)^{k_i} w_i^{r_i} of the state chart, ℂ{w} is free over ℂ{p} of rank wt(S). -/
alias supp_boundary_state_family_rank := Multigraph.finrank_stateParamGerms

/-- **`supp:boundary-algebra`** Proved. Setting p = 0 sends the family basis to the monomial basis of
the special fiber ℂ[w]/(w_i^{r_i}). -/
alias supp_boundary_family_special_fiber := Multigraph.stateFiberEquiv_mk_stateFamilyBasis

/-- **`sf:normal-form`, `fig:k4-states`** Proved (statewise complex counts). For small nonzero p the
admissible solutions are partitioned by the state charts, the chart of a state S containing exactly
wt(S) solutions, all simple. -/
alias sf_statewise_chart_counts := Multigraph.exists_statewise_chart_counts

/-- **`real:all-real-states`** Proved. For a_e > 0, a_e ≠ 1 and small positive p, the chart of a
state S contains one real solution if S is Eulerian and none otherwise; all wt(S) chart solutions are
real exactly for cycle unions; a real chart solution of S has negative-edge set S. -/
alias real_all_real_states_chart_counts := Multigraph.exists_statewise_real_chart_counts

/-- **`real:all-real-states`** Proved. The same in every field orthant, through the gauge
transformation of the charts. -/
alias real_all_real_states_orthant := Multigraph.exists_statewise_real_chart_counts_of_orthant

/-- **`fig:k4-states`, `sf:k4-states`** Proved. For K₄ the complex chart count per state is 16 for
K₄, 4 for K₄ − e and 1 for the other states, and the charts partition the 48 solutions. -/
alias sf_k4_statewise_chart_counts := Examples.K4_statewise_chart_counts

/-- **`fig:k4-states`, `real:all-real-states`** Proved. For K₄ the real chart count per state is 1
for the 8 Eulerian states and 0 otherwise, 8 real roots in total. -/
alias sf_k4_statewise_real_counts := Examples.K4_statewise_real_chart_counts

/-- **`thm:structure` (Cohen–Macaulay), `supp:cm-localization`** Proved. The incidence ring is
Noetherian and at every prime P its localization has depth equal to its Krull dimension (Mathlib's
Ext depth), both equal to the height of P. The proof passes the existence of maximal-length regular
sequences from polynomial rings to the finite free parameter algebra, instead of localizing the
resolution. -/
alias alg_cohenMacaulay_all_primes := Multigraph.incidence_cohenMacaulay_all_primes

/-- **`alg:pencil-sections`** Proved. For d_G > 0 and a finite-quotient parameter tuple the pencil
section M_G is finite free over ℂ[X] (acting through the last parameter form) of rank ω̃_G(1). -/
alias alg_pencil_finite_free := Multigraph.incidencePencil_finite_free

/-- **`alg:pencil-sections`** Proved. The pencil section is a one-dimensional Cohen–Macaulay ring:
Noetherian, of Krull dimension 1, with depth equal to dimension at every prime. -/
alias alg_pencil_cohenMacaulay := Multigraph.incidencePencil_cohenMacaulay

/-- **`alg:pencil-sections`** Proved. Its coefficient ring, S_G cut by the first d_G − 1 coefficient
forms, is a polynomial ring in ρ + 1 variables, over which the pencil section is finite. -/
alias alg_pencil_coefficient_ring := Multigraph.incidencePencilCoefficientEquiv

/-- **`alg:pencil-sections`** Proved. The pencil section is finite over that polynomial ring in
ρ + 1 variables and Cohen–Macaulay of dimension one. -/
alias alg_pencil_cohenMacaulay_over_coefficients :=
  Multigraph.incidencePencil_cohenMacaulay_over_coefficients

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved (vertex maps, algebra side). On a state whose active vertices φ
does not identify, the Tor map of a vertex map carries the local basis indices along the bijection of
active vertices, with the sign of the induced order change of the active vertices; colliding states
go to zero (`alg_vertex_map_collision_zero`). -/
alias alg_vertex_map_tor_state_formula :=
  Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceTorFullState_vertexMap_apply_of_injOn

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `alg:cycle-product`** Proved. In degree zero, z_C goes to the sign of the
order change on the vertices of C times z_{φ(C)} when φ is injective on them. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_cycle_sign := Multigraph.VertexMap.cycleAlgebraHom_X_eq

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex maps, geometric side). The coordinate map
a_φ : (ℙ¹)^W → (ℙ¹)^V, (x_w) ↦ (x_{φ v}), as a morphism of schemes. -/
alias alg_vertex_scheme_map := Multigraph.vertexSchemeMap

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex maps, geometric side). The pullback of a twist sheaf
along a_φ is the twist sheaf with the summed twist, glued from pulled-back chart frames. -/
alias alg_vertex_twist_pullback := Multigraph.vertexTwistPullbackIso

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Partial (vertex maps, geometric side). The map of exterior bundle
cohomology induced by a_φ (the exact inverse image of abelian sheaves, Ext functoriality and the
comparison with the module pullback). -/
alias alg_vertex_map_exterior_pullback := Multigraph.VertexMap.exteriorCohomologyPullback

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved on colliding pieces (vertex maps). On the
edge-set component of a state whose active vertices φ identifies, both sides of the naturality
square vanish, so the square commutes there unconditionally. -/
alias alg_tor_isomorphism_vertex_map_collision :=
  Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceTorExteriorEquiv_vertexMap_of_not_injOn

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved auxiliary (vertex maps). The naturality
square from the multi-twist state formula for the pullback; the formula is
`alg_vertex_map_twist_state_formula` and the unconditional square
`alg_tor_isomorphism_vertex_map_natural`. -/
alias alg_tor_isomorphism_vertex_map_natural_of :=
  Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceTorExteriorEquiv_vertexMap_of

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved auxiliary (vertex maps). The multi-twist state formula for the
pullback along a_f: on twists whose support f does not collide, the pullback of twist cohomology acts
on state coordinates by the pulled-back index with the sign `vertexMapSign`, in every degree. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_twist_state_formula := Multigraph.vertexMapTwistStateFormula

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved (vertex maps). The Tor isomorphism with
exterior bundle cohomology is natural for vertex maps that may identify vertices: the Tor map induced
by the incidence ring map corresponds to the pullback of exterior cohomology along a_φ. -/
alias alg_tor_isomorphism_vertex_map_natural := Multigraph.VertexMap.incidenceTorExteriorEquiv_vertexMap

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved (vertex maps). The exterior state formula of the pullback: zero
on colliding states, and the pulled-back state with the sign `vertexMapSign` otherwise. -/
alias alg_vertex_map_exterior_state := Multigraph.VertexMap.exteriorCohomologyState_pullback

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `supp:functoriality`** Proved. A graph map (vertex map, edge map with
reversal flags and orientation signs ε_φ, compatible with endpoints) copies the coefficients with
signs, and the substitution sends the edge relation of e to ε_φ(e) times that of φ(e): the paper's
a_φ^* b_e = ε_φ(e) b_{φ(e)}. -/
alias alg_graph_map_relation := Multigraph.GraphMap.torusPolyHom_incTorusRel

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. The induced algebra map of incidence rings is compatible with the
coefficient ring map. -/
alias alg_graph_map_incidence := Multigraph.GraphMap.incidenceHom_coeffHom

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. The incidence ring maps respect composition of graph maps. -/
alias alg_graph_map_incidence_trans := Multigraph.GraphMap.incidenceHom_trans

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. The Tor maps, defined intrinsically as derived ring maps, respect
composition of graph maps. -/
alias alg_graph_map_tor_trans := Multigraph.GraphMap.incidenceTorHom_trans

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. For every factorization of a graph map into a vertex map and a
signed edge map, its Tor map is the composite of the factors' Tor maps. -/
alias alg_graph_map_tor_factorization := Multigraph.GraphMap.incidenceTorHom_eq_of_factorization

/-- **`alg:functoriality`, `alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved. The Tor isomorphism with exterior bundle
cohomology is natural for graph maps, the coefficient rings changing along the graph map. -/
alias alg_tor_isomorphism_graph_map_natural := Multigraph.GraphMap.incidenceTorExteriorEquiv_graphMap

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved (over ℂ). The induced maps of exterior bundle cohomology respect
composition of graph maps. -/
alias alg_graph_map_exterior_trans := Multigraph.GraphMap.exteriorCohomologyMap_trans

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved auxiliary. The natural coefficient-degree-n piece of 𝒰_G is the
eigenspace of the coefficient scaling c ↦ a c with eigenvalue a^n (one scalar a = 2 suffices); no
edge order is involved. -/
alias alg_coefficient_piece_scale := Multigraph.mem_incidenceCoefficientPiece_iff_scale

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. The incidence ring map of a graph map is a graded algebra map for
the natural coefficient grading, compatible with identities, composition and the factorization. -/
alias alg_graph_map_graded := Multigraph.GraphMap.incidenceGradedHom

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. The disjoint-union isomorphism carries the degree-n piece of
𝒰_{G⊔H} (edge order Sum.Lex on E ⊕ F) onto the sum of the tensor products of the pieces of 𝒰_G and
𝒰_H of total degree n. -/
alias alg_disjoint_union_graded := Multigraph.map_incidenceCoefficientPiece_disjointSum

/-- **`alg:functoriality`** Proved. Degreewise, the degree-n piece of 𝒰_{G⊔H} is the direct sum over
i + j = n of the tensor products of the degree-i piece of 𝒰_G and the degree-j piece of 𝒰_H. -/
alias alg_disjoint_union_piece_equiv := Multigraph.incidenceSumPieceEquiv

/-- **`supp:cm-localization`** Proved auxiliary (general). Over a local ring, a finite module with a
finite free resolution of length ℓ has depth at least depth A − ℓ (the depth lemma along the
syzygies, Mathlib's Ext depth). -/
alias supp_depth_finite_free_resolution :=
  ResolutionTools.localDepth_sub_length_le_of_finite_free_resolution

/-- **`supp:cm-localization`** Proved (the depth bound). Localizing the free resolution of length ρ at
a prime 𝔭 of S_G gives depth_{(S_G)_𝔭}(𝒰_G)_𝔭 ≥ ht 𝔭 − ρ. -/
alias supp_cm_localization_depth := Multigraph.incidence_localized_depth_ge

/-- **`supp:cm-localization`** Proved (bounds). For primes containing the kernel of S_G → 𝒰_G the
localized module is nonzero and ht 𝔭 − ρ ≤ depth ≤ dim. -/
alias supp_cm_localization_bounds := Multigraph.incidence_localized_depth_bounds

/-- **`supp:cm-localization`** Proved. For every prime 𝔭 ⊇ I = ker(S_G → 𝒰_G), the support
dimension of (𝒰_G)_𝔭 over (S_G)_𝔭 equals ht 𝔭 − ρ. -/
alias supp_cm_localization_dimension := Multigraph.incidence_localized_supportDim

/-- **`supp:cm-localization`** Proved. For every prime 𝔭 ⊇ I, depth (𝒰_G)_𝔭 = ht 𝔭 − ρ = dim (𝒰_G)_𝔭:
𝒰_G is a Cohen–Macaulay S_G-module at every prime of its support. -/
alias supp_cm_localization_cohenMacaulay := Multigraph.incidence_localized_cohenMacaulay

/-- **`supp:cm-localization`** Proved. The prime I = ker(S_G → 𝒰_G) has height ρ. -/
alias supp_cm_localization_height := Multigraph.height_ker_coeffHom

/-- **`alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved (normalization). In every bidegree, the Tor class with a single
state basis vector goes to the exterior cohomology class with the same state vector, coefficient +1.
This fixes the normalization: naturality, products and units alone do not exclude rescaling by λ^p.
It holds by construction of the state-basis isomorphism; the independent check is that the
base-change isomorphism, built without state bases, equals it (`alg_zero_base_change_eq`). -/
alias alg_tor_isomorphism_normalization := Multigraph.incidenceTorExteriorEquiv_stateClass

/-- **`alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved (normalization). A rescaled map c • Φ agrees with Φ on a state
class only for c = 1. -/
alias alg_tor_isomorphism_normalization_scalar := Multigraph.smul_incidenceTorExteriorEquiv_stateClass_eq_iff

/-- **`alg:tor-isomorphism`, `alg:k4-resolution`** Proved example in positive Tor degree. For K₄ and the
five-edge state in bidegree (p, q) = (1, 5), the Tor class goes to the exterior class with the same
state, whose cell cocycle has the Laurent monomial t₀⁻¹t₁⁻¹t₂⁻¹t₃⁻¹ with coefficient +1. -/
alias alg_k4_tor_normalization := Examples.K4_torNormalization_fiveClass

/-- **`alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved example. The cell cocycle of the K₄ test class. -/
alias alg_k4_tor_normalization_cocycle := Examples.K4_torNormalization_cocycle

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved (construction). The universal Koszul complex `K_G` over
`S_G`: a chain complex of sheaves of modules on `(ℙ¹)^V × Spec S_G` with terms the exterior
bundles `∧^k F_G^∨` (homological degree `k` is cohomological degree `−k`) and differential the
contraction with the universal section `s^univ`. -/
noncomputable alias alg_universal_koszul_complex := Multigraph.incUniversalKoszulComplex

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved. The differential squares to zero. -/
alias alg_universal_koszul_d_comp := Multigraph.univKoszulDifferential_comp

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved. `K_G` is exact in every negative cohomological degree, as a
complex in the abelian category of sheaves of modules. -/
alias alg_universal_koszul_exact := Multigraph.incUniversalKoszulComplex_exactAt

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved. On a standard chart the differential of `K_G` is the graded
Koszul differential of the chart incidence equations. -/
alias alg_universal_koszul_chart := Multigraph.incUniversalKoszul_chart

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved. The graded Koszul complex of a weakly regular sequence is
exact in positive degrees (regular implies Koszul-regular). -/
alias alg_koszul_exact_of_regular := Multigraph.gradedKoszul_exact_of_isWeaklyRegular

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved (augmentation on charts). On each standard chart the cokernel
of `∧^1 F_G^∨ ⟶ ∧^0 F_G^∨` is the chart ring of the projective zero scheme: the augmentation is
surjective and its kernel is the image of the differential. -/
alias alg_universal_koszul_chart_augmentation := Multigraph.incUniversalKoszulChartAugmentation_exact

/-- **`alg:resolution`** Proved (Čech model). The Čech–Koszul total complex of the sections of `K_G`
for the product of the standard two-chart covers is `S_G`-linearly isomorphic to the total complex
of the resolution, compatibly with the differentials. -/
alias alg_universal_koszul_cech_equiv := Multigraph.univCechKoszulEquiv_differential

/-- **`alg:resolution`** Proved (Čech model). The isomorphism preserves the internal degree. -/
alias alg_universal_koszul_cech_internal := Multigraph.univCechKoszulEquiv_mem_internalPiece

/-- **`alg:resolution`** Proved (Čech model). The cohomology of the Čech–Koszul total complex of
`K_G` vanishes in every total degree `n ≠ 0`. -/
alias alg_universal_koszul_cech_exact := Multigraph.univCechKoszul_exact_of_ne_zero

/-- **`alg:resolution`** Proved (Čech model). In total degree zero the cohomology of the Čech–Koszul
total complex of `K_G` is `𝒰_G`, `S_G`-linearly. Its comparison with the derived global sections
is `alg_resolution_derived_cech`. -/
noncomputable alias alg_universal_koszul_cech_h0 := Multigraph.univCechKoszulH0Equiv

/-- **`alg:resolution`** Proved (derived global sections, vanishing). The hypercohomology
H^n((ℙ¹)^V × Spec S_G, K_G) = Hom_{D(Ab)}(ℤ, K_G[n]), defined in the derived category of abelian
sheaves for any model of it, vanishes for n ≠ 0. -/
alias alg_resolution_derived_vanishing := Multigraph.incUniversalKoszulHypercohomology_eq_zero

/-- **`alg:resolution`** Proved (derived global sections in degree zero). H^0(K_G) ≅ 𝒰_G, linearly
over S_G, where S_G acts on H^0 through the geometric scalars of the exterior bundles. -/
noncomputable alias alg_resolution_derived_h0 :=
  Multigraph.incUniversalKoszulHypercohomologyZeroLinearEquiv

/-- **`alg:resolution`** Proved (comparison). The hypercohomology of K_G is computed by the
cohomology classes of morphisms from the Čech resolution of ℤ for the product of the standard
two-chart covers, i.e. by the Čech–Koszul total complex. -/
noncomputable alias alg_resolution_derived_cech := Multigraph.incUniversalKoszulHypercohomologyEquiv

/-- **`alg:resolution`** Proved (normalization of hypercohomology). For a sheaf placed in degree
zero, the hypercohomology is Mathlib's sheaf cohomology `Sheaf.H`. -/
noncomputable alias sheaf_hypercohomology_single := Multigraph.sheafHypercohomologySingleEquiv

/-- **`supp:nonnormalizable-dim`** Proved (tree case). For a connected tree there is a nonzero
P ∈ ℤ[a,b] such that over every field, for a_e² ≠ 1 and P(a,b) ≠ 0, no solution with nonzero
messages, nonzero update denominators and F_i = −1 at every vertex exists. -/
alias supp_nonnormalizable_dim_tree := Multigraph.supp_nonnormalizable_dim_tree

/-- **`supp:nonnormalizable-dim`** Proved (ν ≥ 1). For a connected graph with ν ≥ 1 there is a
nonzero P ∈ ℂ[a,b] such that for P(a,b) ≠ 0: a_e² ≠ 1, the locus F ≡ −1 is nonempty, and at
every point of it the Jacobian of the chart equations is surjective, its kernel has dimension
ν − 1, and the implicit function theorem gives a local chart onto an open subset of a
(ν − 1)-dimensional space. -/
alias supp_nonnormalizable_dim_cyclic := Multigraph.supp_nonnormalizable_dim_cyclic

/-- **`supp:nonnormalizable-dim`** Proved (chart). For a_e² ≠ 1 the locus F ≡ −1 is in bijection,
through x_e = y_{(e,false)}, with the chart fiber {x : x_e ≠ 0, a_e, 1/a_e, b_i Φ_i(a,x) = −1}. -/
alias supp_nonnormalizable_chart := Multigraph.nonnormalizableChartEquiv

/-- **`supp:nonnormalizable-dim`** Proved (smoothness over every field). For a connected graph
there is a nonzero P ∈ ℤ[a,b] outside whose zero set every point of the locus is a regular point
of the chart equations. -/
alias supp_nonnormalizable_regular := Multigraph.nonnormalizable_regular

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (chain level). ℂ ⊗_{S_G} of the Čech–Koszul total complex
is the Čech complex of ⊕_q ∧^q F_G^∨ on X_G over ℂ: the base change of the total differential is
the Čech differential. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_model := Multigraph.zbcBaseChangeEquiv_differential

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved. The Koszul differential becomes zero at the coefficient
origin. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_koszul := Multigraph.zbc_baseChange_koszul

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (Tor). Tor_p^{S_G}(𝒰_G, ℂ)_q is the cohomology of the
base-changed Čech model in internal degree q, through the base change of the perturbation data,
without state bases. -/
noncomputable alias alg_zero_base_change_tor := Multigraph.zbcTorEquiv

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (sheaf cohomology). The cohomology of the base-changed Čech
model is the actual sheaf cohomology H^{q−p}(X_G, ∧^q F_G^∨), without state bases. -/
noncomputable alias alg_zero_base_change_sheaf := Multigraph.zbcSheafEquiv

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (the composite). The isomorphism
Tor_p^{S_G}(𝒰_G, ℂ)_q ≅ H^{q−p}(X_G, ∧^q F_G^∨) obtained by base change to the coefficient
origin. -/
noncomputable alias alg_zero_base_change_iso := Multigraph.zbcExteriorEquiv

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`, `alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved (agreement). The isomorphism obtained
by base change equals the state-basis isomorphism `alg_tor_isomorphism`, as linear equivalences:
the two constructions give the same map, with no sign or rescaling. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_eq := Multigraph.zbcExteriorEquiv_eq

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (normalization). The base-change isomorphism sends the Tor
class of every state to the exterior class of the same state, with coefficient +1. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_stateClass := Multigraph.zbcExteriorEquiv_stateClass

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved (augmentation). The augmentation ∧^0 F_G^∨ ≅ 𝒪_Y → i_*𝒪_{Z_G}
of the universal Koszul complex, a morphism of sheaves of modules on Y = (ℙ¹)^V × Spec S_G. -/
noncomputable alias alg_universal_koszul_augmentation := Multigraph.incKoszulAugmentation

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved. ∧^1 → ∧^0 → i_*𝒪_{Z_G} is exact as a sequence of sheaves. -/
alias alg_universal_koszul_augmentation_exact := Multigraph.incKoszulAugmentation_exact

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved. The cokernel of ∧^1 → ∧^0, as a sheaf, is i_*𝒪_{Z_G}. -/
noncomputable alias alg_universal_koszul_cokernel := Multigraph.incKoszulCokernelIso

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved ("this complex resolves 𝒪_{Z_G}"). The augmentation is a
quasi-isomorphism from the universal Koszul complex to i_*𝒪_{Z_G} in degree zero. -/
alias alg_universal_koszul_resolves := Multigraph.incKoszulAugmentationChainMap_quasiIso

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved. On each chart the augmentation has the values of the chart
augmentation onto the chart ring of the zero scheme. -/
alias alg_universal_koszul_augmentation_chart := Multigraph.incZeroChartSectionsIso_augmentation

/-- **`alg:universal-koszul`** Proved. On global sections the augmentation lands in Γ(Z_G, 𝒪) ≅ 𝒰_G
with the chart values of the chart model. -/
alias alg_universal_koszul_augmentation_global :=
  Multigraph.incKoszulAugmentation_globalSections_chart

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle`, `supp:vector-bundle`** Proved (total space). Z_G is isomorphic
to the total space of the rank-3m vector bundle glued from Spec Sym of the kernel frames on the face
cover of X_G, with the transposed kernel transitions. -/
noncomputable alias alg_vector_bundle_total_space := Multigraph.incSymZeroIso

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle`** Proved. The isomorphism lies over X_G. The projection of Z_G
to X_G is defined through the glued incidence scheme (on a chart it forgets the coefficients,
`incidenceProjectiveZeroChartToScheme_projection`); the package has no morphism (ℙ¹_{S_G})^V →
(ℙ¹_ℂ)^V. -/
alias alg_vector_bundle_total_space_projection := Multigraph.incSymZeroIso_projection

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle`** Proved. The isomorphism matches the zero sections. -/
alias alg_vector_bundle_zero_section := Multigraph.incidenceProjectiveZeroZeroSection_incSymZeroIso

/-- **`alg:incidence-vector-bundle`** Proved. The isomorphism matches the maps to the coefficient
space Spec S_G. -/
alias alg_vector_bundle_coefficient := Multigraph.incSymZeroIso_coefficient

/-- **`supp:vector-bundle`** Proved. The projection of the glued total space is affine. -/
alias alg_vector_bundle_affine := Multigraph.incSymProjection_isAffineHom

/-- **`supp:vector-bundle`** Proved. Over each face the sections of the total space form the
symmetric algebra (a polynomial ring in 3m variables) over the face ring. -/
noncomputable alias alg_vector_bundle_sym_sections := Multigraph.incSymFaceSectionsIso

/-- **`supp:vector-bundle`** Proved. Its restriction maps are the transposed kernel transitions. -/
alias alg_vector_bundle_sym_restrict := Multigraph.incSymFaceSectionsIso_restrict

/-- **`supp:vector-bundle`** Proved. The coordinate transitions are the transposes of the transitions
of the kernel sheaf K. -/
alias alg_vector_bundle_sym_transpose := Multigraph.incSymRestrict_X_kernelSheaf

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (homotopy equivalence over S_G). The free resolution F⁻ and the
Čech–Koszul total complex C are homotopy equivalent as complexes of S_G-modules, through the
perturbation data ι, P and −H. -/
noncomputable alias alg_zero_base_change_homotopy_equiv := Multigraph.zbdHomotopyEquiv

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (the derived equivalence). Base change to ℂ of this homotopy
equivalence gives an isomorphism in D(ℂ) between ℂ ⊗ F⁻, which computes 𝒰_G ⊗^L ℂ, and
C₀ = ℂ ⊗ C. No flatness is used. -/
noncomputable alias alg_zero_base_change_derived := Multigraph.zbdDerivedIso

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved. C₀ is the Čech complex of ⊕_q ∧^q F_G^∨ on X_G over ℂ with
zero Koszul part, whose cohomology is the sheaf cohomology (`alg_zero_base_change_derived_cohomology`);
RΓ(X_G, ⊕_q ∧^q F_G^∨[q]) as an object of D(ℂ) is represented by this Čech model. -/
noncomputable alias alg_zero_base_change_derived_model := Multigraph.zbdDerivedModelIso

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved. In degree −p the cohomology of C₀ is the product over q of the
cohomology of the base-changed model, which is sheaf cohomology. -/
noncomputable alias alg_zero_base_change_derived_cohomology := Multigraph.zbdDerivedCohomologyEquiv

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (by construction). On a Tor class the derived isomorphism
induces the existing base-change map on cohomology: both sides are the base change of ι. The
substantive comparison is `alg_zero_base_change_derived_exterior`. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_derived_tor := Multigraph.zbdDerivedIso_torClass

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`, `alg:tor-isomorphism`** Proved. On cohomology the derived isomorphism
is the Tor isomorphism `alg_tor_isomorphism`. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_derived_exterior := Multigraph.zbdDerivedIso_exterior

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved. Every state class goes to the exterior class of the same
state with coefficient +1, in every bidegree. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_derived_stateClass := Multigraph.zbdDerivedIso_stateClass

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (the derived products). The derived base change respects the
products, for Mathlib's monoidal tensor product of complexes: in D(ℂ), the product μ on ℂ ⊗ F⁻
followed by the derived isomorphism `alg_zero_base_change_derived_model` equals β ⊗ β followed by
the Čech–Koszul product ∪₀ : C₀ ⊗ C₀ ⟶ C₀ (`alg_zero_base_change_cech_product`), where
β : ℂ ⊗ F⁻ ⟶ C₀ is the base change of ι followed by the model isomorphism, whose image in D(ℂ) is
the derived isomorphism. The product μ on ℂ ⊗ F⁻ is the specialized standard Tor product (the
specialization of the multiplication lift `incResolutionCup`, which computes `incidenceTorProduct`
by `incidenceTorProduct_eq_transferred`), read on the tensor product through the identification of
ℂ ⊗ F⁻ with the state model and of the tensor product of the state model with the pair model
(`alg_zero_base_change_pair_tensor`). On cohomology this square is
`alg_zero_base_change_derived_product_cohomology`. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_derived_product := Multigraph.zbdDerivedTensorProduct

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved. The same square out of the tensor product of the state
model `S = ℂ ⊗ F⁻` with itself: Q(μ) ≫ Q(ι₀) = Q(ι₀ ⊗ ι₀) ≫ Q(∪₀), with ι₀ the specialized
inclusion `zbcContraction.i`. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_derived_product_square := Multigraph.zbdTensorProductSquare

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved. The zero-differential pair model of pairs of states, through
which `alg_zero_base_change_derived_product_pair` compares the products, is Mathlib's monoidal
tensor product `S ⊗ S` of the state model with itself, by `finsuppTensorFinsupp'` on every summand
`S.X i₁ ⊗ S.X i₂`. -/
noncomputable alias alg_zero_base_change_pair_tensor := Multigraph.zbdPairTensorIso

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved. The Čech–Koszul product ∪₀ of the base-changed model C₀ is
a chain map C₀ ⊗ C₀ ⟶ C₀ out of Mathlib's tensor product of complexes: on every summand
C₀.X i₁ ⊗ C₀.X i₂ it is the product `zbcTotalCup` over ℂ, and the chain-map property is the
Leibniz rule with the signs ε₁ = 1, ε₂ = (−1)^{i₁} of `ComplexShape.up ℤ`
(`zbcTotalCup_leibniz`, `zbcSign_degree`). -/
noncomputable alias alg_zero_base_change_cech_product := Multigraph.zbdModelCupHom

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved. Specialization at the coefficient origin carries the
Čech–Koszul product over S_G to the product ∪₀ over ℂ; the Leibniz rule over ℂ follows from the
one over S_G through the surjective specialization. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_specialize_product := Multigraph.zbcSpecialize_totalCup

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved. The chain map ∪₀ ∘ (ι₀ ⊗ ι₀) out of the pair model is the
identification of the pair model with the tensor product followed by ι₀ ⊗ ι₀ and ∪₀. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_pair_cup_factor := Multigraph.zbdPairTensorHom_cup

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (products, through the pair model). The derived isomorphism
carries the product of the zero-differential state model to the product of the base-changed Čech
model, as an equality of morphisms in D(ℂ) out of the pair model of pairs of states; since the pair
model has zero differential and free terms, this equality is equivalent to the comparison on
cohomology. It is the form of `alg_zero_base_change_derived_product` before the identification of
the pair model with the tensor product. -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_derived_product_pair := Multigraph.zbdDerivedProduct

/-- **`alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (products on cohomology). -/
alias alg_zero_base_change_derived_product_cohomology := Multigraph.zbdDerivedIso_product

/-- **`alg:resolution`** Proved (sign-corrected chain isomorphism). With the integer signs
t_m = (−1)^{m(m+1)/2}, the comparison of the Hom complex out of the Čech resolution of ℤ into K_G
with the Čech–Koszul total complex is an isomorphism of cochain complexes. -/
noncomputable alias alg_universal_koszul_hom_cech_iso := Multigraph.zbdHomCechIso

/-- **`alg:free-terms`** Proved. The p-th free term of the resolution is S_G-linearly isomorphic to
⊕_{p ≤ q ≤ m} S_G ⊗_ℂ H^{q−p}(X_G, ∧^q F_G^∨), with the actual Ext-defined sheaf cohomology. The
generator of a state goes to 1 ⊗ the exterior class of the same state, so the isomorphism depends
on the free basis; its reduction modulo (S_G)_+ is canonical (`alg_free_terms_residue`). -/
noncomputable alias alg_free_terms := Multigraph.incFreeTermCohomologyEquiv

/-- **`alg:free-terms`** Proved (the grading S_G(−q)). An element of F_p has internal degree n iff,
for every q, the q-summand of its image lies in (S_G)_{n−q} ⊗_ℂ H^{q−p}. -/
alias alg_free_terms_internal := Multigraph.incFreeTermCohomologyEquiv_mem_internal_iff

/-- **`alg:free-terms`** Proved. The generator of the state (S, κ) goes to 1 ⊗ its exterior class in
the summand q = |S|. -/
alias alg_free_terms_stateGenerator := Multigraph.incFreeTermCohomologyEquiv_stateGenerator

/-- **`alg:free-terms`, `alg:zero-base-change`** Proved (canonical modulo (S_G)_+). Reducing the
q-summand of the image of x along S_G → ℂ gives the base-change isomorphism, built without state
bases, applied to the internal-degree-q component of the Tor class of x. -/
alias alg_free_terms_residue := Multigraph.incFreeTermCohomologyEquiv_residue

/-- **`alg:resolution`** Proved (the two routes to 𝒰_G agree). Postcomposing a class of H^0(K_G)
with the augmentation K_G → i_*𝒪_{Z_G}[0], reading it as Mathlib's H^0 = global sections and
applying Γ(Z_G, 𝒪) ≅ 𝒰_G gives the identification H^0(K_G) ≅ 𝒰_G through the Čech–Koszul model. -/
alias alg_resolution_derived_h0_augmentation :=
  Multigraph.incidenceProjectiveZeroGlobalSectionsEquiv_hypercohomologyZeroSections

/-- **`alg:resolution`** Proved. The same for the S_G-linear form of H^0(K_G) ≅ 𝒰_G. -/
alias alg_resolution_derived_h0_augmentation_linear :=
  Multigraph.incidenceProjectiveZeroGlobalSectionsEquiv_hypercohomologyZeroSections_linear

end BPFixedPoints.Paper
